name 'building-data-driven-systems-preassessment-q6_2025'

question 'Why should a developer use a "helper function" to handle an array operation like `.push()` instead of just calling `.push()` directly in the main code?'

right 'Helper functions allow you to include validation logic (like checking if the data is valid) before updating the collection.'
wrong 'JavaScript requires every array method to be wrapped in a function to work.'
wrong 'Functions make the code run significantly faster by reducing memory usage.'
wrong 'It prevents the AI from being able to read or suggest changes to the data.'

allow_multiple_attempts false

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 3

Wrapping operations in helper functions promotes "defensive programming." It allows you to check for errors or empty data before it is added to your main collection.
MARKDOWN
